 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "In the kitchen of Claude Monet, the veteran cooks haze new recruit Denis by making him shave and boil coconuts, right before owner Dmitry Nagiyev walks in with news of a late-night banquet.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "denis",
   "t": "Я побрил кокосы, что дальше?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А теперь свари их.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "denis",
   "t": "Что мы вообще готовим?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Варёные кокосы, чего непонятно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ребята, есть хорошая новость.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "И есть плохая новость.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я вас не очень люблю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сегодня не расходимся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У нас импровизированный банкет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Работаем дружным коллективом всю ночь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Что вы носы повесили?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Всем будет хорошая премия!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through each line of the kitchen hazing and Nagiyev's announcement.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "denis",
   "t": "Я побрил кокосы, что дальше?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I shaved the coconuts, what is next?' The perfective past verb with prefix 'po-' shows Denis actually completed the absurd task of shaving coconuts.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А теперь свари их.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And now boil them.' The singular imperative tells him to cook the coconuts in boiling water.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "denis",
   "t": "Что мы вообще готовим?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What are we even cooking?' The adverb meaning 'in general' or 'at all' expresses Denis's growing suspicion.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Варёные кокосы, чего непонятно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Boiled coconuts, what is unclear?' The past passive participle functions as an adjective meaning 'boiled'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ребята, есть хорошая новость.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Guys, there is good news.' In Russian, 'news' is a countable feminine singular noun when referring to one piece of news.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "И есть плохая новость.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And there is bad news.' The feminine adjective 'bad' agrees with the singular noun 'news'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я вас не очень люблю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I do not love you very much.' Putting the negative particle before the adverb 'very' softens the statement to 'not very much'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сегодня не расходимся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We are not going home today.' The reflexive verb with prefix 'raz-' literally means to disperse in different directions.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У нас импровизированный банкет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We have an impromptu banquet.' A borrowed long adjective modifies the masculine noun 'banquet'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Работаем дружным коллективом всю ночь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We are working as a friendly team all night.' The instrumental case without a preposition expresses working 'as a friendly team', followed by the accusative time span 'all night'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Что вы носы повесили?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why have you hung your noses?' Hanging one's nose is the classic Russian idiom for looking gloomy or crestfallen.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Всем будет хорошая премия!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everyone will get a good bonus!' Using the dative plural 'to everyone' with 'will be' announces a reward for the whole crew. Now listen to the whole exchange again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "denis",
   "t": "Я побрил кокосы, что дальше?",
